<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canaan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Canaanite</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Canaan is the ancient name for the region of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, roughly corresponding to present-day Israel, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. Its city-states were brought under Egyptian control by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> and remained a dependency of the Egyptian Empire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> for much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a>. Canaanite culture also gave rise to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canaan.jpg" alt="Canaan" width="320" height="513" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philip Schaff · No restrictions · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_dictionary_of_the_Bible.._(1887)_(14781539332).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
